# The author's working config: copied into the repo root but never committed.
# The committed template is `cxf.toml.example`. Ignored (rather than merely
# untracked, as in the old repo) so a stray `git add -A` cannot publish local
# provider keys. The legacy name stays ignored too: an upgraded installation
# may still carry `config.toml` (the resolver falls back to it with a warning).
